{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q19861011","formula":"Na₅(UO₂)(SO₄)₃(SO₃OH)(H₂O)","hill":"H3Na5O19S4U","elements":["H","O","Na","S","U"],"composition":{"H":3.0,"O":19.0,"S":4.0,"U":1.0,"Na":5.0},"names":{"en":"Meisserite","uk":"Майссерит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Meisserite is a very rare uranium mineral with the formula Na5(UO2)(SO4)3(SO3OH)(H2O). It is interesting in being a natural uranyl salt with hydrosulfate (hydroxysulfate) anion, a feature shared with belakovskiite. Other chemically related minerals include fermiite, oppenheimerite, natrozippeite and plášilite.","uk":"Майссери́т — дуже рідкісний мінерал урану з формулою Na5(UO2)(SO4)3(SO3OH)(H2O). Він цікавий тим, що є природною ураніловою сіллю з гідросульфатним аніоном, що є спільною рисою з бєлаковськіїтом. Інші хімічно споріднені мінерали включають ферміїт, оппенгаймерит, натро-ципеїт і плашиліт."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1195125","atoms":70,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.438,0.0,0.0],[-0.197,11.661,0.0],[-1.83,-3.051,13.228]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":-0.099,"y":5.831,"z":0.0,"el":"Na"},{"x":-1.929,"y":2.78,"z":13.228,"el":"Na"},{"x":5.34,"y":5.831,"z":0.0,"el":"Na"},{"x":3.51,"y":2.78,"z":13.228,"el":"Na"},{"x":0.784,"y":5.084,"z":12.027,"el":"Na"},{"x":2.627,"y":3.526,"z":1.201,"el":"Na"},{"x":-0.915,"y":-1.525,"z":6.614,"el":"Na"},{"x":-1.112,"y":10.136,"z":6.614,"el":"Na"},{"x":4.523,"y":-1.525,"z":6.614,"el":"Na"},{"x":4.326,"y":10.136,"z":6.614,"el":"Na"},{"x":3.926,"y":3.636,"z":9.96,"el":"Na"},{"x":-0.515,"y":4.975,"z":3.268,"el":"Na"},{"x":-1.128,"y":7.133,"z":8.913,"el":"Na"},{"x":4.539,"y":1.477,"z":4.315,"el":"Na"},{"x":0.577,"y":-2.278,"z":11.731,"el":"Na"},{"x":2.834,"y":10.889,"z":1.497,"e